marting@rhino.qpsx.oz.au ("Martin Gregory") writes:

>The topic of the day is RUST.  What is its effect?  Is it better to
>wield an ordinary dagger or a blessed thoroughly rusty +4 wakizashi?
>Similarly with armour - I see that the AC drops, but is it still worth
>wearing?  Can rust be fixed?

You have probably noticed that there are three degrees of rustiness:
rusty, very rusty and thoroughly rusty.
For armors, being rusty seems to have the same effect as subtracting 1 
from the enchantment, very rusty equals -2 for enchantment and 
thoroughly rusty equals -3. 
I believe it is the same with weapons.
You can easily see if the rusty piece of armor is still worth wearing
by simply taking it off and checking the effect on your Ac.
(Though you may still want to wear rusty gauntlets of power for strength
or any gloves for cockatrice corpses, thoroughly rusty shield of reflection,
or some other items with special abilities. I have never seen even thoroughly
rusty pieces of armor make my Ac worse than it would be without the item,
unless it has negative enchantment..)

And yes, rust CAN be fixed!

Enchant the rusty armor/weapon while you are confused. The rust disappears
and the armor/weapon becomes rustproof!
(When fixing rusty armor you might want first to remove all non-rusty
pieces of armor to ensure that the rusty one will be the one that the
scroll affects.. and if you have both blessed and uncursed scrolls of
enchantment, use the uncursed one for rustproofing and the blessed one
when you are not confused. Blessing doesn't give you any bonus when you're
confused.)
